{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pulls/28696","id":4494641538,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABC-bJgg","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/28696","diff_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/28696.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/28696.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/28696","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pulls/28696/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pulls/28696/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/28696/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/statuses/b12818a24407175d941e9299e7b5fb7874a654d9","number":28696,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"convert : add DeepSeek V4.1 (DeepseekV41ForCausalLM)","user":{"login":"vcruz305","id":16494159,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDk0MTU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16494159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305","html_url":"https://github.com/vcruz305","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Overview\n\nAdds conversion support for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (`DeepseekV41ForCausalLM`) by subclassing the existing V4 model, under its own `deepseek41` architecture. Most of the V4 path carries over unchanged.\n\nDifferences that needed handling:\n\n- Text parameters are nested under `text_config`, so they are promoted in `index_tensors`. Overriding `load_hparams` does not work, because `ModelBase.__init__` calls it explicitly rather than through the instance.\n- `num_hash_layers` is absent in V4.1 while the V4 path reads it unconditionally.\n- The FP8 scale block size is `[32, 32]` rather than `[128, 128]`. V4 hardcodes 128, and reusing that value rescales every dequantized weight without raising, so the block size is now read from `quantization_config`.\n- Indexer `k_norm` and `wk` map onto the existing `INDEXER_K_NORM` and `INDEXER_ATTN_K`. `attn.compressor.ape` and `attn.indexer.compressor.*` are absent in V4.1 and go unused.\n- Four new tensors for the engram conditional memory.\n\nThe two engram tables need a separate write path. Each is `384,006,168 x 256`, and the inherited FP8 dequant computes `weight.float() * scale` over the whole tensor, which is about 393 GB as float32 for one table. They are read in row blocks from the safetensors shard, quantized per block, and accumulated into a disk backed memmap. Their scale layout also differs: `[rows, 8]`, one scale per 32 columns of a single row, rather than the `[rows/32, cols/32]` tiling the linear weights use.\n\n## The architecture name\n\nAn earlier revision of this PR rode on `MODEL_ARCH.DEEPSEEK4` and added the engram tensors to V4's own list. That was wrong twice over, and it now declares `deepseek41` instead. `DEEPSEEK4` is left untouched.\n\n**Convention.** llama.cpp does not mirror the HF `model_type`, it drops the `_v`: `deepseek_v2` became `deepseek2`, `deepseek_v3.2` became `deepseek32`, `qwen2_moe` became `qwen2moe`. Only 10 of the 150 arch strings in `constants.py` contain an underscore at all, so vLLM's `deepseek_v41` would be the odd one out here.\n\n**Correctness.** V4.1 emits `attn_kv_a_norm`, which `DEEPSEEK4`'s declared tensor list does not contain, so the old output did not conform to the architecture it claimed.\n\n**Failure mode.** V4.1 ships the per-layer `hc_attn_{fn,base,scale}` and `hc_ffn_{fn,base,scale}`, 40 of each, but none of `output_hc_fn`, `output_hc_base` or `output_hc_scale`. Routing a V4.1 file to the V4 loader therefore produces a confusing partial match rather than a clean refusal.\n\n`deepseek41`'s tensor list is the 39 families the converter actually writes, derived by reverse mapping them through `TENSOR_NAMES` rather than by trimming V4's list. Against `DEEPSEEK4` it drops `HC_HEAD_{FN,BASE,SCALE}`, `FFN_GATE_TID2EID`, `ATTN_KV_NORM`, `ATTN_COMPRESSOR_APE`, `INDEXER_COMPRESSOR_*` and all six `NEXTN_*`, and adds the four engram entries plus `ATTN_KV_A_NORM`.\n\nDraft, because this is the conversion half only. There is no `deepseek41` runtime yet, so a converted file does not load. Posting it now so the tensor naming can be looked at before more files are produced against it.\n\n## Additional information\n\nConverted `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash` end to end on one machine with 121 GiB of RAM: 1046 tensors, 507.9 GB at `--outtype q8_0` with MXFP4 experts, peak host memory under 8 GB above baseline. Output checked with `GGUFReader`, all 8 engram tensors present. Quantized further to Q2_K and Q3_K_M to confirm the file is well formed downstream. `Q2_K_S` and `IQ2_M` both report that they need an imatrix, which is not obtainable until the model runs.\n\nMeasured rung sizes, for anyone estimating: Q8_0 staging 473.1 GiB (1046 tensors), Q2_K 246.3 GiB, Q3_K_M 323.4 GiB. Those ratios read high against the staging file because it is not uniformly Q8_0: routed experts land as MXFP4, so parts of the ladder move up rather than down. At Q3_K_M the expert down projection goes MXFP4 to q5_K and grows from 2295 to 2970 MiB.\n\n## Requirements\n\n<!-- IMPORTANT: Please do NOT delete this section, otherwise your PR may be rejected -->\n\n- I have read and agree with the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- AI usage disclosure: YES. An AI coding assistant was used to write the converter subclass in `conversion/deepseek.py`, the tensor and architecture entries in `gguf-py/gguf/constants.py`, and the registry line in `conversion/__init__.py`, and to draft this description. The design decisions, the debugging that produced them, and the end to end conversion runs were directed and verified by me, and I am responsible for every line submitted.\n","labels":[{"id":11336651494,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAACo7eS5g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/labels/conversion","name":"conversion","description":null,"color":"ededed","default":false}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-10T10:23:42Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T12:51:17Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"3517eecb7fc1534437e81941c610f7b806c151f6","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"vcruz305:feat/deepseek-v41-convert","ref":"feat/deepseek-v41-convert","repo":{"id":1309620258,"node_id":"R_kgDOTg84Ig","name":"llama.cpp","full_name":"vcruz305/llama.cpp","owner":{"login":"vcruz305","id":16494159,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDk0MTU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16494159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305","html_url":"https://github.com/vcruz305","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcruz305/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.co